    {
      "id": "256",
      "type": "writeup",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 256,
        "body_ja": "",
        "body": "<p><span data-gp-id='376'>たとえば</span> (or <span data-gp-id='376'>例（たと）えば</span> in its kanji form) is an adverb in Japanese that is used at the beginning of a sentence, or an individual statement, in order to present an example. It can be translated almost directly as 'for example'.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='180720'>\r\n<li data-study-question='180721'></ul>\r\n\r\n<section class='funfact'><h4>Fun Fact</h4>\r\n<p><span data-gp-id='376'>例（たと）えば</span> should primarily be used when the 'example' that is being given is as simple as possible. If you want to explain something in further (in-depth) detail, 詳（くわ）しく 'in full' would be used as the adverb instead.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='183989'></ul></section>"
      }
    },
